{
 "id": "253-29",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "One of the key practices we follow is avoiding the use of formatters when writing code.",
  "It's important to format your code manually and not rely on automatic tools.",
  "This fosters a deeper understanding of the code and ensures a consistent style throughout the project.",
  "Another important practice is the use of annotations for functions.",
  "Always include them, even if they may seem redundant at first glance.",
  "By following these practices, you'll not only align with our team's standards but also develop good habits that will benefit your coding skills in the long run.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns.",
  "We're all here to support each other and create high-quality software together.",
  "It's important to have a clear understanding of how your work will be assessed.",
  "It's important to actively participate in these programs, as they provide visibility to your work and can lead to greater opportunities within the company.",
  "First, always include a single digit in function argument names.",
  "Secondly, always use docstrings in your functions.",
  "Docstrings provide a concise description of the function's purpose, arguments, and return values.",
  "To achieve that, I want you to start incorporating a formatter into your Python coding right away.",
  "It will ensure consistency and make your code easier to understand and collaborate on.",
  "That way, you don't even have to think about it, and your code will always be nicely formatted.",
  "Usually, it's as simple as setting up a shortcut or enabling a formatting option.",
  "That way, it becomes a seamless part of your coding process."
 ],
